WEBVTT

NOTE Generated with faster-whisper base.en; source=videos/Workshop/Diabetic/5.2 Near Visual Acuity + Dispense Glasses - PEC_220p.mp4; sourceLang=en; task=transcribe

1
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.706
This video demonstrates how to assess near-vision and dispense glasses.

2
00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:09.014
Wash your hands and don PPE.

3
00:00:09.014 --> 00:00:16.706
You will need near-vision chart, pen and clinical notes, range of reading glasses and a 40cm long piece of string.

4
00:00:16.706 --> 00:00:19.783
Explain what you're going to do in-game consent.

5
00:00:19.783 --> 00:00:22.860
Sit the patient comfortably in a well-lit place.

6
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:28.629
Use a string to make sure the chart is held at the correct 40cm distance.

7
00:00:28.629 --> 00:00:32.860
Ask them to read down the chart with both eyes together.

8
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.200
smallest line they can read comfortably.

9
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.100
If they cannot read the N8 line then try with

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.371
plus 1.5 diopter sphere glasses.

11
00:00:41.371 --> 00:00:46.820
If they still cannot read N8 then use the next higher power

12
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.242
and so on until they can comfortably read N8 text.

13
00:00:50.242 --> 00:00:52.980
Make sure the glasses fit ok and the

14
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.980
patient is happy with their appearance.
